{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggaQhuMa1Q7SX5C1zMqt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The high-spin → low-spin change happens at **Dq ≈ 1 792 cm⁻¹** (10Dq ≈ 17 920 cm⁻¹), from a full d⁵ calculation with configuration interaction.\n\n**Approach.** The crossover is the Dq where the high-spin ground state ⁶A₁g (t₂g³e_g²) and the lowest low-spin state ²T₂g (mostly t₂g⁵) have the same energy.\n\n**1. Single-configuration estimate.** If each state is treated as one pure configuration:\n- E(⁶A₁g, t₂g³e_g²) = 10A − 35B + 0·Dq\n- E(²T₂g, t₂g⁵) = 10A − 20B + 10C − 20Dq\n\nSetting these equal gives Dq = 0.75B + 0.5C = 465.75 + 1425.5 = **1 891 cm⁻¹**.\n\nThis estimate is too high. The ²T₂g level mixes with other ²T₂g terms from higher configurations, which pushes it down. The ⁶A₁g level does not shift, because it is the only sextet.\n\n**2. Full calculation with mixing included.**\n- I diagonalised the full d⁵ Hamiltonian (all 252 microstates), including electron repulsion and the octahedral ligand field, at B = 621 cm⁻¹ and C = 2 851 cm⁻¹.\n- As a check, at zero ligand field it puts the first excited free-ion term (⁴G) at 10B + 5C = 20 465 cm⁻¹ above ⁶S, which is the correct value.\n- I compared the sextet ground state with the lowest doublet as Dq increases. The energy gap ⁶A₁g − lowest doublet is −5 621 cm⁻¹ at Dq = 1 500 and +4 036 cm⁻¹ at Dq = 2 000.\n- The two levels cross at **Dq = 1 791.8 cm⁻¹**. In units of B this is Dq/B ≈ 2.89, or Δ/B ≈ 28.9.\n\nThe single-configuration formula therefore overestimates the crossover by about 100 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1792, \"B\": 621, \"C\": 2851, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full d5 ligand-field diagonalisation gives the 6A1g/2T2g crossing at Dq ≈ 1792 cm^-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1603,"cache_read_input_tokens":4199,"cache_creation":{"e